# EcoSuit-AS — Asteroid-superalloy plate derivative
**Feedstock: main-belt M / S / C bodies (Mars–Jupiter)**
**Same suit architecture: rear-entry HUT, internal exo, step-in, CUP-SM analog, dorsal pack**
**New OML: mined Fe–Ni (and upgraded superalloy), not Shuttle-tile ceramic**

Paper growth article. Not a Psyche claim ticket and not a method to refine a horizon.

---

## 0. Split from EcoSuit MK.I

| | EcoSuit MK.I | EcoSuit-AS |
|---|---|---|
| Where the plates are born | Earth kiln + hemp shop | Belt melt / roll / HIP, or Earth shop using returned metal |
| OML | Silica / alumina ceramic, black/white coats | Fe–Ni to Ni-base superalloy faces |
| Core | Hemp / PI sandwich (SIP) | Grade-dependent: hemp kept, or metal foam / honeycomb |
| Why | Strain isolation under brittle TPS | Ductile metal can take bearing; isolation still wins on fatigue |
| First use | LEO / lunar worn article | Belt yard, Mars transfer, long EVA on metal-rich bodies |

Do not scrap the hemp traveler. AS Grade A can still hang on the same spider. Grade C does not need hemp for strain; it may still want a thermal break.

