## 2. Three plate grades (freeze these names)

### Grade A — Meteoritic plate (first article)
**Alloy:** Fe–(5–8)Ni after melt + slag (P, S, silicates out). Optional 0.2–0.5% C if you have a C-type carbon dump and want a steel, not a stainless.

**Process:** collect → crush → magnetic / density split → melt → slag FeS + phosphide + silicate → deoxidize → cast slab → hot roll / stamp facets → age or leave as-cast → passivate.

**Plate:** 1.2–2.5 mm face, faceted Iron Man language, overlapping scales.
**Core:** keep MK.I hemp / PI, 6–10 mm, ADH-F analog rated for metal IML (not ceramic densify).
**Why hemp stays:** rolled FeNi still prints welds and thermal strain into a HUT. SIP is still cheap.

**Use:** belt-yard EVA, unpressurized cover, first worn metal set.
**Not for:** 1500 °C leading edge. This is structural metal, not HRSI.

### Grade B — Belt stainless / Fe–Ni superalloy-adjacent
**Alloy target:** Fe–18Cr–8Ni class **or** Fe–Ni + Cr + small Mo, if and only if Cr is imported or extracted from S-type chromite-bearing silicates (hard, low yield).

**Process:** Grade A melt + alloy addition + AOD/VOD analog in vacuum + roll + solution treat + optional light cold work.

**Plate:** 1.0–2.0 mm.
**Core:** hemp still legal; metal honeycomb from the same FeNi is the growth core.

**Use:** long-life vacuum OML, hatch ring skins, pack skins, cup outer jacket instead of Inconel-from-Earth.

### Grade C — Ni-base superalloy face (true “superalloy plate”)
**Alloy target:** 718-class or simpler solid-solution Ni–Cr (600-class) if Nb is unavailable.

**Feed math (honest):** to put 55% Ni in the plate you either
- concentrate Ni from many tonnes of 7% Ni metal (Mond / carbonyl or vacuum refining), or
- import Ni-rich taenite separates (20–65% Ni phases exist in irons — tetrataenite / taenite — and can be sorted).

Cr, Al, Ti, Mo, Nb are **alloying imports** unless a separate silicate / pallasite / Earth tanker exists. Do not write “Psyche = 718” on a drawing.

**Plate:** 0.8–1.5 mm face, possible thermal-barrier coat (silicate from C/S slag, not Shuttle tile).
**Core:** Ni foam or FeNi honeycomb. Hemp optional as thermal break only.
**Use:** hot nozzles on Case C hopper, cup wall, hatch ring, anywhere MK.I already called Inconel 718.

