## 3. Architecture on the body

Same datums as MK.I chest traveler (A HUT sternum, B sagital, C hatch).
OML facet (Grade A/B/C metal) → bond primer / flexible isolator (or braze land on Grade C) → core (hemp Grade A/B, metal foam Grade C) → backing (S-glass or FeNi sheet) → Ti / FeNi doubler + inserts → HUT / spider

Changes from ceramic MK.I:

| Item | Ceramic MK.I | AS |
|---|---|---|
| Face thickness | 2.5–4 mm ceramic | 0.8–2.5 mm metal |
| Densified IML | Required | Replaced by grit + primer or nickel strike |
| Edge | Chamfer ceramic | Hem / laser-weld scale overlap |
| Fastener land | Never in face | Still never in thin face — doubler only |
| V-EBM | Bonds to ceramic back | Bonds to metal back; watch creepage |
| Repair | Scrap the tile | Weld / patch a scale |
| Thermal | Face is the TPS | Face needs coating or it is a radiator |

Sternum cup: Grade C wall is the point of the derivative. CUP-IN becomes belt-melt 718-analog or FeNi + imported Cr. CAP-S becomes a metal cap with the same 118 / 72 mm envelope. Hemp still stops at the sealed land.

