## 4. Mine-to-plate process (belt yard)
prospect (radar albedo + sample assay) → anchor / bag / cut → crush to < 10 mm → magnetic drum + eddy + density ├─ FeNi metal   → melt stream ├─ FeS / schreibersite → slag / P-control ├─ silicate     → slag, oxygen, possible Cr/Mg later └─ C-type fines → carbon, water if any, organics → vacuum or inert melt → slag + deox → (Grade B/C) alloy additions → cast slab or atomize → roll / stamp / HIP / AM → heat treat → facet machine + overlap hem → coat (passivate / TBC) → serial + NDE → ship to suit shop (same bond traveler as MK.I, metal primers)
Mond / carbonyl Ni is the historical way to pull nickel out of FeNi as a gas and drop it as powder. That is how you climb from 7% Ni toward Grade C without pretending the asteroid was already 718. It is a plant, not a backpack.

Energy: melt heat is the yard’s problem. A worn suit does not smelt.

