## 5. Plate manufacturing (suit shop, Grade A first article)

1. Receive serialized slab or coil. Assay Ni, Co, P, S, C. Reject high S.
2. Roll to face gauge. Facet-stamp or laser-cut triangles to the MK.I pattern language.
3. Hem or joggle the overlap (Iron Man scale, not tile step).
4. Grit IML. Nickel strike if you are bonding hemp + ADH-F.
5. Core: same hemp traveler as MK.I (moisture gates, edge seal, no hemp in the cup bore).
6. Backing: BK-SG or a 0.5 mm FeNi sheet from the same heat.
7. Doubler: FeNi or leftover Earth Ti. S1–S4 from the same jig.
8. Bond or mechanical stand-off. Metal faces can take more peel than ceramic — still keep a flexible line if the core is hemp.
9. NDE: dye, UT, conductivity map (Widmanstätten leftover is a feature, not a crack — learn the difference).
10. Serial AS-PLT-CHEST-xxx to heat number.

First article: three-facet plastron + one scale, Grade A, hemp core, dummy HUT, 2 × Case A on the spider.

