## 6. What the superalloy actually buys

| Load | Ceramic MK.I | Grade A FeNi | Grade C Ni-base |
|---|---|---|---|
| 6 g Case A | Face is passenger | Face can take some in-plane | Face + cup are structure |
| Micrometeoroid | Ceramic shatter / plug | Ductile dish, weld repair | Better |
| Re-entry plasma | Designed for it | Melts | Melts unless coated and the trajectory is not Earth peak heating |
| Belt EVA cold | Fine | Fine; watch DBTT on low-Ni heats | Fine |
| Hot hopper plume | Keep off hemp | Keep off hemp | Legal on yoke nozzles |
| Mass at equal stiffness | Light face, thick core | Heavier face | Heavier still unless thinned |

Earth→Moon stress test does not change. Metal plates do not give you 15 km/s. They give you a plate you can weld in a yard 4 AU out.

